    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Belknap-Campus/Professor-Term--Open-Rank--and-Director-of-the-Noble-H-Kelley-Psychological-Services-Center--PSC-_R109499": {
      "title": "Professor Term (Open Rank) and Director of the Noble H. Kelley Psychological Services Center (PSC)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Psychology Location: Belknap Campus Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Term (Fixed Term) Job Req ID: R109499 Position Description: The Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences at the University of Louisville invites applications for a Professor Term (Open Rank) and Director of the Noble H. Kelley Psychological Services Center (PSC). The start date is June 1, 2027. The PSC is a training clinic located on campus and operated by the university’s APA-accredited Ph.D. program in Clinical Psychological Science. Clinical services are provided by Ph.D. students supervised by licensed psychologists in Kentucky with the Health Service Provider (HSP) designation. The PSC operates as a fully functioning psychological clinic, providing services for children, adolescents, and adults to the university and the larger metropolitan community on a sliding scale basis. Services include individual, family, group, and couples psychotherapy as well as psychological assessments. More information about the PSC can be found on the website: https://artsandsciences.louisville.edu/academics-programs/academic-departments/psychological-and-brain-sciences/services/psychological-services-center The Director position is a full-time, 12-month clinical Term faculty position and includes administrative (60%) and supervision and teaching (40%) responsibilities. The Director works collaboratively with program faculty, staff, and the department chair in overseeing clinic operations and has an essential role in training graduate students. The Director would provide clinical supervision in empirically supported interventions and assessments as well as teach graduate courses to Ph.D. students in the program. Examples of courses include Professional and Ethical Issues in Clinical Psychology, Clinical Psychopathology, History of Modern Psychology, and Assessment. The Director would also be responsible for: maintaining compliance with ethical, legal, licensing, insurance, and accreditation regulations as well as maintain up to date clinical knowledge; coordinating faculty supervisors and training and supervising clinic staff; coordinating the program Colloquium series; overseeing the budget and engaging in fiscal planning; maintaining and developing connections with referral sources; leading outreach activities; coordinating external practicum placements for students; assisting with PSC clinical team placements for students; assisting with coordination of student evaluations and clinical competencies; and assisting with accreditation reporting requirements. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. from an APA-accredited and/or PCSAS-accredited program in Clinical Psychology, Clinical Psychological Science, or Clinical Science or related field APA-accredited internship in Clinical Psychology Must be license eligible in Kentucky at time of hire, licensed by Kentucky as soon as possible or within 6 months of hire date with the Health Service Provider (HSP) designation, and must maintain an active license and HSP status. Applicants who are not yet licensed as a psychologist in Kentucky should review the requirements for licensure and the Health Service Provider designation to ensure they can meet these requirements: https://psy.ky.gov/ Applicants must be authorized to work in the U.S. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of high-quality clinical supervision in empirically-supported practices. Evidence of high-quality teaching, ideally at the graduate level or demonstration of potential in this area. Evidence of administrative or similar leadership experience or demonstration of potential in this area. Application Requirements – submit as one PDF on the application website Cover letter describing interest in and fit for the position, including description of any administrative or similar leadership roles and/or abilities Curriculum Vitae, including Kentucky license number and HSP status if available Clinical statement describing clinical interests and experiences and efforts to maintain current knowledge (two pages maximum) Teaching statement describing graduate teaching interests and experiences, including clinical supervision and evidence of effectiveness if available (e.g., teaching evaluations) (two pages maximum) Graduate program(s) transcript(s) Contact information (name, degree, position title, e-mail address, phone number) for three professional references Review of applications will begin immediately. All applications received by November 2 at 11:59pm EST will receive full consideration. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
    },
    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Remote/Program-Manager-III---KY-MEP-Client-Services_R109506": {
      "title": "Program Manager III - KY-MEP Client Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Location: Remote Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Job Req ID: R109506 Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in a related field and eight (8) years of relevant experience or the equivalent combination of education and experience. Grade 9 (Salaried). Position Description: The Kentucky Manufacturing Extension Partnership (KY-MEP), a leading business consultancy dedicated to educating and empowering Kentucky manufacturers, is seeking an experienced Program Manager II - KY MEP Client Services to cover the state of Kentucky.  KY-MEP is focused on solving real-world manufacturing challenges through tailored strategies in workforce leadership and culture, operational efficiency, growth and innovation, and automation technologies. KY-MEP has delivered over $717 million in total impact over five years, including significant cost savings, new investments, and sales growth for manufacturers. This is a renewable grant-funded position supported by a 10-year award, currently in its fifth year. Continued employment is contingent upon the availability and renewal of grant funding.   This position is ideal for a seasoned transformational sales professional with strong manufacturing expertise, and responsible for leading territorial efforts to engage and serve Kentucky's manufacturing community—from small businesses to industry leaders—by developing and selling KY-MEP's comprehensive consulting and training services.   The KY-MEP office is based at the JD Nichols Campus for Innovation and Entrepreneurship in downtown Louisville.   We solve manufacturing problems. https://louisville.edu/kymep   Essential Duties and Responsibilities Proposal Writing: Develop comprehensive scope of work based on client reviews, observations, and discussions to deliver custom tailored KY-MEP solutions. Growth Orientation: Identify, evaluate, and implement expansion activities aligned with KY-MEP's focus on innovation and sustainable revenue growth. Continuous Improvement: Uncover and eliminate non-value-added activities from operations, leveraging proven and innovative approaches to enhance results. Self-Motivation: Maintain organization, attention to detail, and task focus to independently drive KY-MEP's mission of empowering manufacturers. Project Management: Organize tasks, delegate responsibilities, and follow up to ensure successful implementation of consulting and training programs. Analytical Skills: Evaluate data and information to develop optimal solutions for manufacturing challenges in growth, automation, workforce, and operations. Team Orientation: Collaborate by serving, leading, mentoring, and following others to advance KY-MEP processes, programs, and client outcomes. Interpersonal Relations: Build trust-based relationships with manufacturing clients, employees, colleagues, management, and vendors through effective communication. Work Ethic: Exhibit motivation, diligence, and persistence to complete tasks efficiently in support of KY-MEP's high-impact services. Critical Thinking and Flexibility: Analyze issues, identify options, and adapt quickly in a dynamic environment with interruptions to meet client needs. Delivery and Client Interaction: Ability to deliver quality programming while cultivating meaningful client trust and interactions. Outbound Sales and Support: Lead and track sales activities, coordinate student workers in marketing support, and collaborate cross-functionally with partners to achieve KY-MEP goals in manufacturer support and statewide impact. Collaborate cross-functionally with program leads, university departments, and external partners to support KY-MEP goals and initiatives.   Preferred Qualifications 3+ years’ experience as an outreach/direct sales representative in a B2B environment. Demonstrated experience interacting with all levels of leaders within a manufacturing facility. Experience in the full sales process; initial cold call through executed agreement. Proven track record of growing sales from direct involvement. Experience within a manufacturing environment. Experienced setting and managing Key Performance Indicators (KPI’s) for success Extensive instate vehicle travel. Ability to stay overnight as needed. Experience with a manufacturing-centric organization such as the Manufacturing Extension Partnership (MEP) or similar. Experience with Salesforce or similar CRM tool. Experience working out of a remote office. Working knowledge of marketing and outreach techniques and best practices. Target Compensation Maximum: $115,989.00 Target Compensation Minimum: $77,326.00 Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
    },
    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Belknap-Campus/Psychologist-IV_R109507": {
      "title": "Psychologist IV",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Location: Belknap Campus Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Job Req ID: R109507 Minimum Requirements: Doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology and two (2) years of experience as a psychological counselor. May require certification in Psychodiagnostics and Autonomous Functioning from the Kentucky State Board of Psychology. Grade 8 (Salaried) Position Description: The Counseling Center within the Division of Student Affairs is seeking to hire a Psychologist IV. The Psychologist provides therapeutic services to students including individual, group, and couples counseling, psychological assessment and crisis intervention and also provides outreach to the campus community at large. Additionally, this position supervises practicum students providing many of these same services. Essential Duties and Responsibilitie s Provide triage; initial assessments; crisis management; and individual, group, and couples counseling to students, in-person and via telehealth and provide psychological assessments as necessary Prepare and maintain records, evaluations, and reports in an accurate and timely manner, in accordance with professional, legal, and ethical standards using the department’s software Consult and collaborate with Campus Health Services providers, Student Affairs staff, various University departments, and third-party agencies as necessary Provide clinical supervision to at least one graduate trainee, including supervision of assessments and practicum students Provide outreach services at University resource fairs, signature University events, and scheduled college and class presentations Serve on divisional and University-wide committees to collaborate with other offices, schools, and colleges to advance the department’s outreach initiatives Assist with other division initiatives and operations such as freshman orientation, Welcome Week, and resident move-in events Perform other duties and complete special projects as assigned Preferred Qualification s Licensure to function autonomously in Kentucky or aligned to obtain Kentucky licensure within 12 months of hire Four (4) years of experience in a clinical or counseling setting inclusive of practicum work Experience working at a college counseling center or community agency, inclusive of conducting psychological assessments Strong organizational skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Experience providing clinical services to students and working on a college campus Ability to provide oversight of departmental programs including coordination of scheduling with staff group leaders, collaboration with other departments on marketing and communication initiatives, and coordination of off-site workshops Ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with colleagues, administration, faculty, staff, students, employers, and the general public Proficient using Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams, PowerPoint) Experience using Titanium scheduling software Please note that any selected candidate's hire date may be effective no earlier than January 5, 2027. Work Hours and Location This is a full-time, exempt position with a 37.5-hour regular workweek. Additional work hours may be required based on department needs, programming, staffing, and/or scheduling. This position works at the Belknap and Health Sciences Campus. Occasional overnight travel (for professional development or conferences) may be required. Employee Benefits The University of Louisville offers competitive benefits and perks to eligible full-time and part-time employees. Please visit the University of Louisville Total Rewards webpages for details. Student Affairs The Division of Student Affairs encourages candidates to apply who have demonstrated the capacity to create supportive work environments, collaborate effectively on teams, and serve the students we admit and aim to attract. Please submit a resume, cover letter, and three professional references with your application. Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
