    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Health-Sciences-Center/Research-Scientist_R109509": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Location: Health Sciences Center Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Job Req ID: R109509 Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in a related field and four (4) years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Grade 7 (Salaried) Position Description: The Brown Cancer Center is seeking a Research Scientist for the Medicinal Chemistry Core Facility.  The incumbent will primarily be responsible for co-designing and synthesizing derivatives for multiple drug discovery programs.  The successful candidate will be part of an interdisciplinary team focused on drug discovery.  The incumbent will learn medicinal chemistry methodology, how to design biologically relevant compounds, and to interpret biological data.  The successful candidate will demonstrate proficiency in synthetic organic chemistry and be capable of searching scientific literature for information on recent developments and for synthetic protocols and conduct all laboratory activities within established safety procedures. Essential Duties: Co-design and synthesize a small library of derivatives and design robust synthetic routes. Maintain a well-kept and accurate laboratory notebook. Help manage the daily operations of the research lab including ordering, maintaining instrumentation, general lab upkeep, compliance with safety regulations, inventory management, and cataloging and storing derivatives. Prepare written reports upon request that document synthetic methodology and prepared derivatives. Assist with manuscript preparation, writing chemistry experimentals and other related duties as assigned. Preferred Qualifications: Medicinal and/or organic chemistry background. Ph.D. Degree in organic or medicinal chemistry and 2 or more years work experience. Proficient in synthetic organic chemistry. The Brown Cancer Center encourages candidates to apply who have demonstrated the capacity to create supportive work environments, collaborate effectively on teams, and serve the students we admit and aim to attract. Target Compensation Maximum: $91,721.00 Target Compensation Minimum: $61,147.00 Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
    },
    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Health-Sciences-Center/Student-Services-Specialist-II_R109383": {
      "title": "Student Services Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Location: Health Sciences Center Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Job Req ID: R109383 Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in a related field and two (2) years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Grade 4 (Salaried) Position Description: The Student Services Specialist II for Medical Students supports the operational functions of the Office of Medical Student Affairs by facilitating student services, coordinating academic records processes, and supporting student-facing programs. This position serves as a central resource for students, faculty, and staff by managing communications, coordinating office processes, and ensuring timely responses to inquiries related to medical student services. The specialist contributes to the effective administration of student records by assisting in the receipt, organization, and processing of grades submitted by academic departments and external partners. Working in collaboration with the Student Records Coordinator, this role supports the accurate entry and maintenance of academic data within PeopleSoft and internal record systems, ensuring timely updates and reliable documentation used for class rank calculations, Medical Student Performance Evaluations (MSPEs), and other institutional reporting. The position also assists in processing verification of medical education requests for School of Medicine graduates. This role provides coordination support for faculty and staff by assisting with scheduling meetings, facilitating travel reimbursement documentation, and supporting routine operational needs that contribute to the efficient functioning of the office. The specialist also assists with drafting and preparing official correspondence on behalf of the Senior Associate Dean for Medical Student Affairs, including letters of good standing, enrollment verifications, jury duty excusal letters, and other institutional communications. In addition, the specialist supports the planning and execution of meetings, student programs, and special events by coordinating logistics such as catering, materials preparation, and event setup. The position maintains records related to student service opportunities and other student engagement initiatives, ensuring accurate documentation and program tracking. Through these responsibilities, the specialist helps maintain organized student information, supports student engagement efforts, and contributes to the effective delivery of services within the Office of Medical Student Affairs. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Serve as a primary point of contact for the Office of Medical Student Affairs by managing routine inquiries received through the office service account and phone lines. Respond to common questions using established information and best practices, and communicate effectively with internal and external stakeholders to route requests to appropriate staff or resources. Support daily office operations by maintaining organized digital and physical records, managing standard document workflows, and assisting with information management tasks. Address routine operational issues using common solutions to support efficient and consistent office functioning. Coordinate scheduling and logistical support for faculty and staff meetings and assist with routine travel reimbursement documentation. Exercise personal judgment within standard procedures to address common scheduling conflicts and administrative needs in collaboration with team members. Assist with planning and logistics for meetings, student programs, and office events by following established practices for catering coordination, material preparation, and event setup. Collaborate with colleagues to ensure programs are delivered smoothly and meet operational expectations. Maintain tracking and documentation for student service initiatives and programs by applying best practices for record‑keeping and routine reporting. Support accurate documentation through consistent organization and attention to standard processes. Support student academic records operations by assisting with the collection, organization, and processing of grades received from academic departments and external partners. Address routine discrepancies using established procedures and communicate with relevant stakeholders as needed. Collaborate with the Student Records Coordinator to support timely and accurate entry of grades into the PeopleSoft system. Use standard practices to assist in maintaining academic records supporting institutional reporting, including class rankings and Medical Student Performance Evaluations (MSPEs). Maintain and organize grade‑related documentation within shared record systems to support routine academic tracking and reporting requirements, ensuring materials are accessible and properly filed. Assist with processing verification of medical education requests for School of Medicine graduates by following established institutional procedures and addressing routine requests using common documentation standards. Draft and prepare official correspondence on behalf of the Senior Associate Dean for Medical Student Affairs, including letters of good standing, enrollment verifications, and jury duty excusal letters, using established templates and exercising judgment to ensure accuracy and appropriateness. Support student engagement and community‑building efforts by assisting with routine student recognition activities, such as preparing birthday acknowledgments and other communications, and collaborating with team members to promote a positive student experience. Preferred Qualifications Preferred work experience in Student Services field.  Experience within a university department or another student-centered industry may be considered. Competencies Proficient in Microsoft Suite, PeopleSoft, Workday. Proficient in CardMed and RedMed. Strong oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to provide clear, detailed, and appropriate responses. Demonstrated ability to build positive working relationships and collaborate effectively with students, faculty, and staff while maintaining collegiality. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision, proactively anticipate needs, and plan accordingly. Detail-oriented with strong organizational skills. Strong commitment to customer service and a passion for supporting medical students. Ability to work effectively as part of a team and contribute to a shared goal. Flexibility and adaptability in a changing medical education environment. Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
    },
    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Health-Sciences-Center/Assistant-Professor-Term_R109365": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Term",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Location: Health Sciences Center Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Term (Fixed Term) Job Req ID: R109365 Position Description:  The Division of Immunotherapy, Department of Surgery at the University of Louisville (UofL) School of Medicine seeks a highly motivated bioinformatician at the Assistant Professor level to join our research program. Division of Immunotherapy, Department of Surgery: The Division of Immunotherapy is a highly functioning collaborative research team that has had an exceptional track record of grant funding and high impact publications. Faculty members in the Division also have associate appointment with other departments such as the Department of Microbiology and Immunology to train graduate students. The newly recruited faculty member will have office space in the Clinical Translational Research Building (CTRB) along with the rest of the Division; it is fully equipped for research in molecular and cellular immunology, including live cell imaging, single cell and spatial genomics, conventional flow cytometry, mass cytometry and imaging mass cytometry (IMC), cell sorting facility, and state of the art animal housing with germ-free facilities and whole-animal imaging capability (PET/CT scanner). Facilities and Research Partners: The UofL School of Medicine provides an outstanding research environment and the majority of the departmental faculty are also members of either the Center for Predictive Medicine (CPM), Center for Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy (CCII), or Center for Functional Microbiomics, Inflammation and Pathogenicity (CFMIP). The current position offers a wide range of resources as well as collaborative research opportunities. The state-of-the-art facilities of the Immuno-Oncology program at the Brown Cancer Center include a biorepository for clinical specimen collection, clinical trial office, and the CyTOF and imaging mass cytometry (Functional Immunomics Core) to comprehensively phenotype immune landscape within the tumor microenvironment. Candidate Requirements: The successful candidate will lead computational analyses of high-dimensional biomedical datasets, including single-cell RNA-seq, single-cell ATAC-seq, spatial transcriptomics/proteomics, CyTOF, bulk RNA-seq, and multi-omics datasets. The candidate is expected to develop collaborative research programs, work closely with immunologists, cancer biologists, clinicians, and computational scientists, and contribute to grant applications, manuscript preparation, and trainee mentorship. The ideal candidate should have strong expertise in R/Python programming, single-cell and spatial data analysis, multi-omics integration, machine learning/statistical modeling, and data visualization. Experience in cancer immunology, immunotherapy, inflammation, or immune profiling is highly desirable. Candidates should hold a PhD or equivalent degree in bioinformatics, computational biology, biostatistics, computer science, genomics, or a related field, with a strong publication record and demonstrated ability to work in interdisciplinary teams. The position offers a competitive salary and a considerable startup package commensurate with qualifications and experience. Louisville, with a population of over one million and the home of the Kentucky Derby, was chosen as one of the top 10 places for families by Parenting magazine in 2010 and as the most livable city in America by the US Conference of Mayors in 2012. It offers excellent private and public schools for K-12 education and University of Louisville Health Sciences Center has Schools of Medicine, Dental Medicine, Public Health, and Nursing. Application Process: Applicants should submit the following documents with the application: 1) a cover letter 2) a summary of present and future research plans 3) curriculum vitae 4) the names/email addresses of three references.    Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
    },
    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Health-Sciences-Center/Assistant-Professor-Term_R109464": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Term",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Anesthesiology Location: Health Sciences Center Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Term (Fixed Term) Job Req ID: R109464 Position Description: The Department of Anesthesiology & Perioperative Medicine at The University of Louisville seeks a professor in Anesthesiology & Perioperative Medicine to serve in a term-track position. This position will begin at the Assistant Professor level. As a faculty member of the medical school staff, based in the Department of Anesthesiology & Perioperative Medicine at University of Louisville Hospital, as well as UofL Healthcare-Jewish Hospital Downtown campus, this position involves instruction of medical students during their rotation in our department and participation in the didactic teaching of anesthesia residents and other surgical and emergency department residents rotating through anesthesiology. This position also involves patient management, supervision of residents and nurses in the OR, and research duties.  Applicants must hold an MD, and must have completed clinical training in anesthesia. Candidate must also possess a Kentucky Medical license. Applicants should attach a cover letter and CV online as well. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
    },
