    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Belknap-Campus/Applications-Administrator-IV--IT-Systems-_R109423": {
      "title": "Applications Administrator IV (IT Systems)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Location: Belknap Campus Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Job Req ID: R109423 Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Business, Computer Science or a related field and six (6) years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Grade 9 (Salaried). Position Description: The University of Louisville is seeking a skilled applications administrator to provide support for our ticketing system, TeamDynamix. This position will be responsible for the configuration, maintenance, and optimization of our TeamDynamix (TDX) platform. This role is critical to ensure the reliability, scalability, and usability of our IT Service Management (ITSM), Project Portfolio Management (PPM), and enterprise workflow automation systems. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams to implement service catalog enhancements, streamline ticket routing, create/maintain workflows, and develop system integrations using TDX iPaaS functionality. Experience with administering ticketing systems, CRM’s, and systems that heavily utilize forms and workflows is a plus. Specific duties related to this position are: Administer and maintain the TeamDynamix platform, including service catalog, ticketing forms, dashboards, workflows, and automation rules. Lead configuration and deployment of incident, service request, and change management forms. Manage user roles, permissions, and group assignments across departments. Develop and maintain integration with third-party systems using TDX iPaaS. Develop reports and dashboards. Maintain and foster TDX vendor relationship. Monitor system performance, troubleshoot issues, and implement improvements. Collaborate with ITSM leads, consultants, and stakeholders to align platform capabilities with business needs. (Implementation of new modules) Support training efforts by creating documentation and walkthroughs for end users and technicians. Ensure data integrity, security, and compliance with university policies and privacy regulations. Participate in planning and execution of platform upgrades and enhancements. Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
    },
    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Belknap-Campus/Assistant-Director--Annual-Giving_R109454": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Annual Giving",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Location: Belknap Campus Time Type: Full time Worker Type: Regular Job Req ID: R109454 Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in a related field and two (2) years experience in fund-raising. Additional experience may not be used to offset the educational requirement. Grade 6 (Salaried) Position Description: The Assistant Director of Annual Giving – Leadership Annual Giving will play a key role – individually and collectively – in identifying and cultivating long-term relationships with donors who have the capacity to make mid to major level gifts, while leveraging the relationships and vision of university leaders to secure support for strategic university priorities and initiatives. The Assistant Director of Annual Giving will be an exceptional team-oriented fundraising professional who will demonstrate a successful track record in identifying, qualifying, and advancing donors through the giving pipeline toward higher levels of support.   The Assistant Director of Annual Giving reports to the Director of Annual Giving. The individual will provide creative and visionary coordination of fundraising endeavors for unit-based and university-wide programs. They will convene campus partners and advise on the development of coordinated, cross-functional strategies to enhance lifetime donor engagement and philanthropic investment. Working collaboratively across Philanthropy & Alumni Engagement (PAE), the Assistant Director will play a key role in strengthening the donor pipeline by identifying and qualifying prospects with the capacity and inclination to give at higher levels. When appropriate affinity and capacity are identified, the Assistant Director will proactively refer donors to major gift teams to support continued growth and long-term philanthropic impact. Duties & Responsibilities   Manage a portfolio of 100-150 individual prospects capable of making 5 figure gifts through identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship cycles.  Forge long-term relationships with these individuals to cultivate their interest in UofL. Actively maintain a portfolio of prospects capable of making $1,000-$25,000 gifts, particularly where there are multiple complex university relationships and the opportunity exists to have university-wide impact that requires thoughtful, experienced, prospect management. Solicit and secure significant gifts to reach a minimum annual goal as determined by PAE leadership Identify and advance qualified donors toward major gift portfolios through proactive collaboration with major gift officers, sustaining a 20–30% referral rate of prospects capable of long-term philanthropy at the $50,000+ level. Collaborate with major gift officers and deans, faculty, program directors, and other university leaders when needed to prepare for prospect meetings, engagement strategies, and solicitations. Complete at least 140 donor and prospect meetings annually to enhance relationships and drive progression along the donor cycle. Record moves management into the CRM database to track engagement with donors. Oversee the preparation of funding proposals, talking points and scripts, assessments of potential support, briefings, gift agreements, and stewardship reports for assigned prospects. Ensure that all interested parties are involved in key efforts focused on specific prospects. Promote deferred giving and have an understanding and expertise in deferred vehicles and the role they can play in supporting visionary gifts. Travel to meet with donors/prospects and execute strategic moves.   Preferred Qualifications 2-3 years of prior work experience in a related field.     Competencies Clear and effective written and oral communication and presentation skills, including individual and large groups. Ability to assess risk combined with a willingness to take calculated risks. A tolerance for the inevitable ambiguity that typifies a large university. Proven ability to drive performance and execute results; strategic and agile thinker to develop opportunities and strategies for organizational success toward objectives. High integrity, judgement, and courage of convictions. Maintain self-awareness, understanding the impact of self on others. Strong evidence of ability to function in an environment of complexity, uncertainty, and change management. Natural sense of curiosity regarding individuals and industry, with the skill to uncover connections, networks, and interests. *Please include a cover letter along with your resume   Philanthropy & Alumni Engagement is committed to creating campus environments that support the success of all students and employees. We believe that employees who feel valued and respected will create policies, programs, practices, research agendas, and services that effectively meet the needs and exceed the expectations of our student population.   Benefits - The University of Louisville has an exceptional benefits package; to learn more about our benefits, please visit  HERE Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
