    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Non-Campus-Other/Seasonal-Bartender-Server---University-of-Louisville-Golf-Club--ULGC---Part-Time-_R109147": {
      "title": "Seasonal Bartender/Server - University of Louisville Golf Club (ULGC) (Part Time)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-14\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Location: Non-Campus Other Time Type: Part time Worker Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Job Req ID: R109147 Minimum Requirements: H.S Diploma or GED and one year of related experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Compliant with all local food safety health codes and required certifications. Position Description: The University of Louisville Golf Club (ULGC) in Simpsonville, KY is hiring Seasonal Bartender/Server. As a Seasonal Bartender/Server you will provide exceptional customer service to club members and guests and will play a crucial role in creating a welcoming atmosphere. You will be responsible for providing prompt, courteous, and enthusiastic service while serving food and beverages to club members and guests during restaurant hours of operation and special events.  Job Responsibilities Take customer orders, serve food and beverages, prepare itemized checks, and accept payments.  Complete all daily tasks and cleaning schedules assigned by the Manager, Food and Beverage (Clubhouse Manager).  Perform daily cash reconciliation.  Prep garnishes for drinks, stock bar, and maintain a clean work area.  Check identification of customers at the bar area to ensure they meet all statutory regulations. Work both Private and Club Events.  Must have good mobility and ability to lift heavy objects; sometimes in excess of 30 pounds.  Must efficiently handle multiple duties under pressure with minimal supervision.  Promote a friendly atmosphere for all Members and guests, as well as coworkers.  Ensure operations comply with all state and federal laws, rules, and regulations, relating to food and beverage sanitation, alcohol and tobacco, and ADA requirements. Perform other duties as appropriate. Preferred Qualifications College degree in Culinary Science, Foodservice Systems Administration/Management, Hotel /Restaurant Management desirable. Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken to ensure equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants for employment. It is the policy of the University that no employee or applicant for employment be subject to unlawful discrimination in terms of recruitment, hiring, promotion, contract, contract renewal, tenure, compensation, benefits, and/or working conditions. No employee or applicant for employment is required to endorse or condemn a specific ideology, political viewpoint, or social viewpoint to be eligible for hiring, contract renewal, tenure, or promotion. Consistent with applicable law, demographic information is collected for aggregate reporting requirements. Demographic information provided through this application is not available to hiring managers/committees and is not considered in hiring or employment decisions. Assistance and Accommodations Computers are available for application submission at the Human Resources Department located at 2315 South First Street Walk, Room 02C - Louisville, Kentucky 40292. If you require assistance or accommodation with our online application process, please contact us by email at  employment@louisville.edu  or by phone 502-852-6258."
