    "https://uofl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UofLCareerSite/job/Belknap-Campus/Intermittent-Temporary-Traffic-Guard---Athletic-Events_R109074-1": {
      "title": "Intermittent Temporary Traffic Guard - Athletic Events",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-07\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Location: Belknap Campus Time Type: Part time Worker Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Job Req ID: R109074 Minimum Requirements: Minimum of high school diploma and one year experience. Minimum of 21 years of age. USA Citizenship at time of appointment. To be eligible for appointment candidates cannot have been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor domestic violence crime as set forth in 18 U.S.C. & 992 (g) (8) and (9). Successful completion of background investigation. Position Description: The Traffic Guard positions will be responsible for directing vehicular traffic and pedestrians at assigned locations, ensuring vehicle and pedestrian safety during University of Louisville athletic events. Job Responsibilities Directs the flow of vehicular and pedestrian traffic at assigned locations. Expedites traffic flow following athletic event to assist with vehicular and pedestrian departures. Direct vehicular and pedestrian traffic during emergencies. Record license plate numbers of vehicles, disregarding traffic laws, and report infractions. Compensation will be commensurate to candidate experience. Equal Employment Opportunity The University of Louisville is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University strives to provide equal employment opportunity on the basis of merit and without unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, sex, age, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, disability, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, veteran status, marital status, or pregnancy. In accordance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Vietnam Era Veteran Readjustment Act of 1974, the University prohibits job discrimination of individuals with disabilities, Vietnam era veterans, qualified special disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, and other protected veterans. The University acknowledges its obligations to ensure affirmative steps are taken